# Redis authentication. Template for .env.redis, which is gitignored.
#
# `make up` GENERATES .env.redis with a random 32-byte password if the file is
# missing — it does not copy this template — so no two deployments share a
# credential and nobody has to remember a bootstrap step. This file exists so
# `docker compose config/build` can parse the topology in a checkout that has
# never run `make up` (CI seeds it exactly the way it seeds .env.ai-proxy).
#
# The password lives in its OWN env file rather than the shared .env because
# compose hands .env to every container: a credential there is a credential for
# intake/eligibility/records/scheduling/interop/roi too. Only redis and the
# gateway (Redis's only client) load this file — guarded by
# tests/test_compose_topology.py.
#
# FAIL-CLOSED: shipped empty on purpose. The redis container refuses to start
# with an empty password rather than fall back to the unauthenticated,
# host-published instance this replaced (docs/debt-log.md D3b), and the gateway
# refuses to connect without one. Generate manually with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
REDIS_PASSWORD=
